On 2009-03-08, Haakon Studebaker <heptapod@gmail.com> wrote:
> I'm going to start a race for NetHack for my own amusement and to further 
> familiarize myself with the sources.
>
> I was wondering if it's possible for a race, regardless of role/class, to 
> have a 50% chance of starting with a specific item? In my case I plan on 
> making a Martian race who will have a 50% chance of starting with a Wand of 
> Probing.

Sure.  Look for the comment "/*** Race-specific initializations ***/"
in src/u_init.c.  Your example case would look something like:

        case PM_MARTIAN:
            /* Martians like to probe things */
            if (rn2(100) >= 50)
                ini_inv(Probing);
            break;

with the "Probing" item defined in the "Optional extra inventory
items" section above, e.g.:

static struct trobj Probing[] = {
        { WAN_PROBING, UNDEF_SPE, WAND_CLASS, 1, 0 },
        { 0, 0, 0, 0, 0 }
};

(Bugs in the code above are possible: I haven't tested it, and I don't
think I've ever looked at that part of the source before today.)

